# What the image does not need, and what it costs to send anyway.
#
# There is no .dockerignore and the build context carried `.git` (250MB) and
# `web/node_modules` (49MB) on every deploy — uploaded, then discarded. The
# second is worse than waste: the web stage installs its own dependencies and
# then `COPY web/ ./` writes the host's tree over them, so whatever was on the
# build machine decided what the image was built against.
#
# `docs/` ships on purpose — `077` records why: the scripts were in the
# container and the eighteen documents they file were not. What does not ship
# is 47MB of *pictures of this system*: the screen sweeps, the UI drive and
# the manual's own screenshots, which no script in the image reads. The
# manual's pictures are served from `web/public/help`, which is inside
# `web/dist`, so the guidebook in the deployment is unaffected. They stay in
# the repository, where the reviews that produced them are read.
#
# `docs/runbook-walk/` deliberately stays: `runbook_guidebook.py` and
# `monday_anchor.py` ship in the image and read it, and a script in the
# container with nothing to read is the defect `077` is named after.

.git
.gitignore
**/node_modules
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
.pytest_cache
.venv
intake/
storage/
web/dist

docs/ui-sweep/
docs/screenshots/
docs/screen-sweep/
docs/audit-ui/
